I've read all the arguments for and against wands of wishing.  My view
is: who cares?  You can make the same argument about finding
"powerful" items in shops.  Should the RNG be tweaked so that good
items are not generated in shops (or have a much lower chance)?  I've
never seen anyone complain about someone's ascension because they
found key pieces of the puzzle in a shop or randomly in an early level
of the dungeon, but when it's a more direct route such as a wand of
wishing-- look out!  While I was trying for a full conduct game as a
Valkyrie, I found +4 dwarvish mithril coat, +5 gauntlets of power, +1
shield of reflection, and +0 cloak of magic resistance in a single
shop on lvl 3 of the dungeon.  This happened about as often as I found
a random wand of wishing (only once).  In the former case, less than
100 turns later, I was bitten by a werecreature and obtained
lycanthropy, turned into a wererat and my polyselfless conduct was
blown.  In the latter case, I went to lvl 51 in under 10-12k turns and
quit because the game was too easy.

I'd say that this should be left as it is.  The early wand of wishing
may or may not help novice players and will definitely help
experienced players who have already ascended (since they know what
lies ahead in the dungeon and what they need to survive/ascend).  If
the novice players ascend due to an early wand of wishing, then I'm
happy for them and they may learn a thing or two for their next
ascension which most likely will not come with a wand of wishing early
on.  For experienced players, they may choose to use it for the fun of
it (or perhaps they are going for fewest number of turns, foodless,
pacifict, or any other strange conduct which needs some amount of
luck) or they may choose not to use it because they want to go
wishless or have an extra challenge of waiting until the castle.  By
the way, any player who gets an early wand of wishing is still not
guaranteed ascension (especially if they are following particular
conducts).  They could still come face to face with a cockatrice (or a
monster wielding a cockatrice corpse), think they are so powerful, and
then die due to stoning because they simply forgot that they didn't
have an item so "insignicant" as a potion of acid or tin of acid
corpse (if they are vegan/vegetarian), or lizard corpse (if no food
restriction).

People want to make the game harder by modifying charges on the wands
of wishing, but those people can simply choose not to use the wishes. 
I'll argue that having an early wand of wishing and not using it is
pretty hard :) (at least the first time you do this, it takes some
self-control).  Note that if you're going illiterate, then you can
only get 2-4 charges from a wand of wishing (depending on how many
charges it is generated with).  If you want to make the game harder,
but still want to use the wand of wishing, why not try illiterate
conduct :)

The point is don't bash on the other people who ascend due to what you
think amounts to luck in getting an early wand of wishing.  The game
is not easy and there are many (creative) ways to die, regardless of
whether or not you obtained your "ascension" kit at dungeon lvl 5.

